    {
      "id": 326,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -5080,
        90
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        380
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "title": "Bulk pictures to one .vox",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Bulk pictures to one .vox\n1. Zip the pictures, named `<anything>-<number>.png` (`hero-1.png`, `hero-2.png`, ... `hero-10.png`), and press **Upload zip** on Load Numbered Image. Uploading resets **index** to `0`.\n2. Press **Run** once. With **whole_zip** on, each finished picture queues the next until the zip is done; keep this window open meanwhile. One picture is processed per run, so memory stays flat.\n\nPictures with alpha use it as their cutout and skip background removal; faint pixels below alpha 32/255 are dropped. Pictures without alpha go through Remove Background.\n\nEach picture is saved as `output/vox/characters/<number>.vox`, and every run rewrites `output/vox/characters.vox` with all of them on a grid, sharing one palette. Re-running a picture replaces its model; use a new collection name for a new set.\n\nThe Download button fetches the multi-model file."
      ]
    }
